---
import BlogPostLayout from "../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro";
import BlogByline from "../../components/BlogByline.astro";
import { PRICING, CHECKLIST, RECURRING_DISCOUNTS, POLICIES, TRUST } from "../../data/claims";

const publishDate = '2026-09-01';
const modifiedDate = '2026-09-01';
const readTime = '6 min read';

const pct = (d: number) => `${Math.round(d * 100)}%`;
const petFee = `$${POLICIES.pets.feePerPet}`;
const shedFee = `+$${POLICIES.pets.heavyShedSurcharge}`;
const cancelFee = `$${POLICIES.cancellation.feeAmount}`;
const travelFee = `$${POLICIES.travelFee.minAmount}–$${POLICIES.travelFee.maxAmount}`;

// FAQ: single source of truth — BlogPostLayout emits the FAQPage schema from
// this array. The visible FAQ section below renders from the same array.
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What should a first quote call include?",
    answer: "Square footage, beds, baths, pets, last real clean, weekly / biweekly / monthly / one-time, and any rooms to skip."
  },
  {
    question: "Is the cheapest quote the right one?",
    answer: "Usually it is the one with the most missing from the list. Read our post on the 3 red flags when hiring a cleaning service."
  },
  {
    question: "Do I have to be home?",
    answer: "No. Code or lockbox is common. Insurance and background checks are why that is not a leap of faith."
  }
];
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title="Questions to Ask a Cleaning Service Before You Hire | Valley Clean Team"
  schemaTitle="Questions to Ask a Cleaning Service Before You Hire"
  description="Ask for a flat quote, a written list of what is not included, proof of insurance, who actually shows up, and the re-clean rule. Here are the questions that matter."
  publishDate={publishDate}
  modifiedDate={modifiedDate}
  faqs={faqs}
>

  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="pt-32 pb-16 px-6 bg-gradient-to-br from-[#1a1a2e] via-[#16213e] to-[#0f3460]">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <div class="text-center">
        <span class="inline-block px-4 py-2 bg-[#FFA985]/20 text-[#FFA985] rounded-full text-sm font-semibold mb-6">
          Hiring Guide
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold mb-6 text-white leading-tight">
          Questions to Ask a <span class="text-[#FFA985]">Cleaning Service</span> Before You Hire
        </h1>
        <div class="mb-8">
          <BlogByline variant="dark" date={publishDate} readTime={readTime} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Article Content -->
  <article class="py-16 px-6">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

        <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Three failures show up before the first mop hits the floor: no flat price, no list of what is skipped, and no one who will come back if they miss a room.
        </p>

        <p>
          We already wrote the short version — arrival windows, no checklist, no insurance — in <a href="/blog/3-red-flags-hiring-cleaning-service" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">3 red flags when hiring a cleaner</a>. This is the list to ask out loud on the quote call.
        </p>

        <p>
          Our published starts: regular <strong>{PRICING.regular.display}</strong>, deep <strong>{PRICING.deep.display}</strong>, move-out <strong>{PRICING.moveInOut.display}</strong>. Recurring: weekly {pct(RECURRING_DISCOUNTS.weekly)} off, biweekly {pct(RECURRING_DISCOUNTS.biweekly)} off, monthly {pct(RECURRING_DISCOUNTS.monthly)} off. <a href="/pricing" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">Pricing</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">1. Is the quote flat, or is it a guess until you see the house?</h2>

        <p>
          Ask: “Is the number you just gave me the number you bill?”
        </p>

        <p>
          Hourly-after-arrival is how invoices grow. A flat quote from square footage and condition is the cleaner version.
        </p>

        <p>
          We quote on the call. That is the bill.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">2. What is not included?</h2>

        <p>
          Ask them to name the outs: inside oven, inside fridge, inside cabinets, laundry, wet-wipe blinds, garage.
        </p>

        <p>
          If they say “we do it all” and will not list exclusions, you do not have a scope. You have a hope.
        </p>

        <p>
          Our regular visit is the {CHECKLIST.standard}-item <a href="/services/house-cleaning" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">house cleaning</a> list. Inside oven and inside fridge belong on <a href="/services/deep-cleaning" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">deep</a> or as add-ons.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">3. Can I see the insurance certificate?</h2>

        <p>
          Ask for the certificate, not a sentence. “We’re covered” is not a document.
        </p>

        <p>
          We carry {TRUST.liabilityCoverageDisplay} in liability. Teams are background-checked.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">4. Who comes — the same people, or whoever is free?</h2>

        <p>
          Ask whether you get a consistent team or a rotating roster. Inconsistent results usually start here, not with “they don’t care.”
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">5. What happens if you miss something?</h2>

        <p>
          Ask for the window and whether the callback is free.
        </p>

        <p>
          Ours: tell us within {TRUST.recleanWindowHours} hours and we re-clean that item at no charge.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">6. What do you charge if I cancel late or you cannot get in?</h2>

        <p>
          Ask for the number. Ours is <strong>{cancelFee}</strong> for cancel inside {POLICIES.cancellation.noticeHours} hours, no-show, or lockout. Cancel with more than {POLICIES.cancellation.noticeHours} hours and there is no fee.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">7. How do you handle keys, codes, and alarms?</h2>

        <p>
          Ask who holds the code, whether it is stored, and what they do if the alarm is set.
        </p>

        <p>
          A lot of our clients are not home. That only works if key handling is boring and written down.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">8. What do you use around kids, pets, and asthma?</h2>

        <p>
          Ask for unscented or <a href="/services/green-cleaning" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">green</a> if that matters. Ask whether it costs extra.
        </p>

        <p>
          For us it does not. Pets themselves do: <strong>{petFee} per pet</strong>, <strong>{shedFee}</strong> when shedding is heavy. Details: <a href="/blog/pet-hair-cleaning" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">pet hair cleaning</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">9. Is the person in my house background-checked and covered by your policy?</h2>

        <p>
          Ask two things: whether everyone who walks in has passed a background check, and whether the company’s liability policy covers damage in your home no matter who on the crew caused it. How a company pays its people is between them and their crew. Whether the person in your kitchen is vetted and covered is your business.
        </p>

        <p>
          Ours are. Every team member is background-checked, and our {TRUST.liabilityCoverageDisplay} liability policy covers damage claims in your home.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">10. Will you put the price, the list, and the date in writing?</h2>

        <p>
          If they will only text “see you Tuesday,” keep looking.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">What we will tell you on the same call</h2>

        <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
          <li>Starting prices and the frequency discount that applies</li>
          <li>Whether you need a deep clean first or can start recurring</li>
          <li>Pet fees if you have animals</li>
          <li>Travel fee of {travelFee} only when it applies, said up front</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          We will not give you a locked size-band chart that pretends every 3-bedroom in Madison County costs the same.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        {faqs.map((faq) => (
          <>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-6 mb-3">{faq.question}</h3>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </>
        ))}

      </div>

      <!-- CTA Section -->
      <div class="mt-16 p-8 bg-gradient-to-br from-[#FFA985]/10 to-[#FFC67D]/10 rounded-2xl border border-[#FFA985]/20 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mb-4">Ask us the list</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">Call and run the questions. If we cannot answer one, that is useful too.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a href="tel:2568261100" class="btn-primary px-8 py-4 rounded-lg font-semibold inline-flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 5a2 2 0 012-2h3.28a1 1 0 01.948.684l1.498 4.493a1 1 0 01-.502 1.21l-2.257 1.13a11.042 11.042 0 005.516 5.516l1.13-2.257a1 1 0 011.21-.502l4.493 1.498a1 1 0 01.684.949V19a2 2 0 01-2 2h-1C9.716 21 3 14.284 3 6V5z"></path></svg>
            Get your price — 256-826-1100
          </a>
          <a href="/request-a-quote" class="bg-white border-2 border-[#FFA985] text-[#333333] px-8 py-4 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-[#FFA985]/10 transition inline-flex items-center justify-center">
            Request a quote online
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mt-6">Tennessee: <a href="tel:6155101427" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">615-510-1427</a></p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

</BlogPostLayout>
